    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d770">

                <pb facs="0757" n="591" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg591"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.5914/26</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Egan </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-06-16T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 16, 1915, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>27. Department is of the opinion that plan suggested in your despatch No. 833,
                    March 8, is desirable and may be feasible and you may very discreetly approach
                    the proper officials with a view to ascertaining whether a proposal such as
                    contemplated would be received not unfavorably.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
